From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:32:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Build the Cubie A7S device tree
 with symbols

The Cubie A7S pin header brings out functions that its device tree
leaves disabled, such as UART and SPI controllers. A user selects them
with a device tree overlay that the boot loader applies, and the overlay
refers to the nodes and pin groups by label. That needs the symbols of
the base device tree.

Compile the board file with -@, as is done for the Pine64 boards.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the board DTB carries the labels of the new
nodes and pin groups, and the test DTBs built from it with an overlay
boot.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
index 8fe64328cbb8..5540aa7b8a26 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ DTC_FLAGS_sun50i-a64-pine64-lts := -@
 DTC_FLAGS_sun50i-a64-pine64 := -@
 DTC_FLAGS_sun50i-a64-pine64-plus := -@
 DTC_FLAGS_sun50i-a64-sopine-baseboard := -@
+DTC_FLAGS_sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s := -@
 
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-a64-amarula-relic.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-a64-bananapi-m64.dtb
